{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5e79eb0c-9871-4d0a-9b37-eee2ee9de987","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Every triangle has three interior angles. Label them alpha, beta, and gamma; we want to find their total.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Angles in a triangle"},{"op":"figure","id":"triangle","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1,7],"y":[-0.8,4.3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[0,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[6,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[2,3],"label":"C"},{"kind":"polyline","id":"outline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"a"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"c"},"r":0.3,"label":"α"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"b"},"from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"a"},"r":0.3,"label":"β"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.3,"label":"γ"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5e79eb0c-9871-4d0a-9b37-eee2ee9de987","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Draw a line through C parallel to AB. Alternate interior angles give matching alpha and beta angles beside gamma.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallel_add","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"parallel","from":[-0.7,3],"to":[6.7,3],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":[-0.7,3],"to":{"at":"a"},"r":0.3,"label":"α"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":[6.7,3],"r":0.3,"label":"β"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"parallel_fact","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\text{Line through C}\\parallel AB"},{"op":"text","id":"matching","anchor":{"el":"parallel_fact","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Alternate interior angles match"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5e79eb0c-9871-4d0a-9b37-eee2ee9de987","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At C, alpha, gamma, and beta fill a straight angle. A straight angle is 180 degrees, so the triangle’s angles total 180 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"straight_add","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"c"},"r":0.9,"start":180,"end":360},{"kind":"text","at":[2,3.55],"text":"180°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"sum","anchor":{"el":"matching","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\boxed{\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=180^\\circ}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Two angles of a triangle are 50° and 60°. What is the third angle?","expected_gist":"70°, because 180° − 50° − 60° = 70°"}}}
